# Buff System Agent Rule

When editing any Buff/Debuff code, data, or docs, follow `docs/design/18-buff-system.md` as source of truth.

## Hard Constraints

- Tick is the primary duration unit.
- Same buff type is stackable.
- On re-apply: add stacks + reset duration.
- Clamp stacks to `max_stacks`.
- Fixed consumption per trigger from buff definition (`consume_layers_fixed`).
- Remove entire buff instance when stacks reach 0.
- Execution order is fixed: filter -> priority sort -> consume check -> consume layers first -> apply effects -> remove if zero.

## Hit Semantics

- For `consume_mode = on_hit_roll_success`, use hit-roll success as the only condition.
- Even if later parried to zero damage, consumption still happens once hit-roll is successful.

## Multi-Hit In One Tick

- A skill can resolve multiple attacks within one tick.
- Each sub-hit must emit a unique event id.
- Buff consumption/effect is evaluated per sub-hit (no merge at tick level).

## Unified Trigger API

- Buff pipeline must be callable by combat, actions, world events, and dialogue.
- Do not add isolated one-off buff entry points for a single subsystem.
- Reuse one shared event context shape and one shared trigger function.

## Register Before Use

- Before introducing any new `event_kind`, `event_name`, or trigger `tag`, register it in `data/editor/buff_event_registry.json`.
- Only after registration should it be used in `data/buffs.json` and runtime trigger calls.
- Avoid runtime-only event names that are not visible in editor registry.

## Debug Visibility

- Detailed buff logs/UI are hidden by default.
- Only show detailed traces when `buff_debug_enabled` is true.

## Implementation Notes

- Reuse existing recalculation flow for stat-affecting buffs (e.g. `recalcCharacterStats()`).
- Prefer indexed lookup by event kind/name to avoid full scan on every event.
- Persist `expires_at_tick` in saves for stable timing.

